prompt:
We're building a lesson reader for an adult-education app (Meridian Learning). Learners read 600-word lessons on tablets and laptops. Our team has three candidate stylesheets for the lesson body and can't agree. Which would you pick, and why? Feel free to suggest small tweaks to your pick.

```css
/* A */ .lesson { max-width: 1100px; font: 14px/1.3 system-ui; color: #444; }
        .lesson h1 { font-size: 15px; } .lesson h2 { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; } .lesson p { margin: 0 0 4px; }

/* B */ .lesson { max-width: 40rem; font: 1.125rem/1.6 system-ui; color: #1f2328; }
        .lesson h1 { font-size: 2rem; line-height: 1.2; margin: 0 0 1.5rem; } .lesson h2 { font-size: 1.375rem; line-height: 1.3; margin: 2rem 0 0.5rem; }
        .lesson p { margin: 0 0 1rem; }

/* C */ .lesson { max-width: 28rem; font: 1.5rem/2.1 system-ui; color: #000; }
        .lesson h1 { font-size: 3.2rem; } .lesson h2 { font-size: 2.4rem; margin: 3rem 0 2rem; } .lesson p { margin: 0 0 2rem; }
```

Here's the stylesheet for the article page of our weekly money newsletter, The Ledger Letter. It's going live tomorrow and I just want a second pair of eyes on the typography. Anything you'd change? Give me the revised CSS if so.

```css
body { margin: 0; background: #fbfaf7; color: #1c1c1c; font-family: Charter, 'Iowan Old Style', Georgia, serif; }
article { max-width: 38rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 1.25rem; font-size: 1.125rem; line-height: 1.6; }
article h1 { font-size: 2.25rem; line-height: 1.15; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
article .byline { font: 0.875rem/1.4 system-ui, sans-serif; color: #5b5b5b; margin: 0 0 2rem; }
article h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.25; margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem; }
article p { margin: 0 0 1.1rem; }
article table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font: 0.9375rem/1.4 system-ui, sans-serif; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
article th, article td { padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #e3e0d8; }
article td.num, article th.num { text-align: right; }
article blockquote { margin: 1.5rem 0; padding-left: 1rem; border-left: 3px solid #b8892b; font-style: italic; }
```
